# Percentage subtraction relative to the left operand

Verifies a percentage on the right of subtraction reads as a fraction of the left operand. Subtracting decimal 50% from plain 100 returns the plain 50.00, while subtracting 10% from 8m preserves the meter unit with 7.20m.

>>> source
const total: decimal = 100
const rate: decimal = 50%
print(total - rate)
const length: decimal = 8m
const discount: decimal = 10%
print(length - discount)

<<< stdout
50.00
7.20m

<<< stderr
